  "notes": [
    "No wildcard build can establish every incompatible profile; execute named batches under the workstation guard.",
    "Language wrappers use a measured two-worker trial under the unchanged 16 GiB guard; restore an affected batch to one worker if needed. Retained DEME preparation remains one worker.",
    "The 26 CUDA implicit/ANCF demonstrations are separate from the qualified explicit Yaris backend.",
    "The python_plotting and python_cad batches declare their real plotting and PythonOCC SDKs and original example targets.",
    "Language batches compile explicit native-library prerequisites at four workers, then generated wrappers and original example assemblies at two workers. Both phases retain eight affinity CPUs, 16 GiB RSS and separate closed receipts. Libraries never increase demo counts.",
    "Observed single-worker peak sampled RSS: NumPy/plot/CAD 5.130 GiB, baseline Python 4.884 GiB, largest managed batch 3.655 GiB. Two-worker qualification remains subject to the existing guard; these observations are not a new resource allowance."
  ]
}
